# System Constraints

A system is not designed in an unlimited environment.

Real-world systems have **constraints** that influence architectural decisions.

### Time Constraints

The system may have a strict deadline.

```text
Example:

Product must launch
within 3 months.
```

### Financial Constraints

The available budget may be limited.

```text
Example:

Limited budget
      ↓
Limited infrastructure
      ↓
Different architecture decisions
```

### Staffing Constraints

The size and skill set of the development team can affect the architecture.

```text
Large Team
    │
    ├── Backend Team
    ├── Frontend Team
    ├── DevOps Team
    └── Security Team


Small Team
    │
    └── A few developers
```

A complex architecture may not be appropriate if the team does not have enough people or expertise to operate it.

